Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: override UNKNOWN layer dataspace for YUV conversion

When a layer has UNKNOWN dataspace (common with vendor camera HAL and
video decoder), the RenderEngine defaults to BT.601 YUV-to-RGB
conversion coefficients. This causes:
- Camera preview green tint (sensor-native colors without CCM)
- Video pink/washed-out tint (BT.709 content decoded with BT.601)

Force UNKNOWN dataspaces to V0_SRGB so the GPU uses BT.709
conversion coefficients, which is correct for most modern content.
This is especially important when the display is in SRGB mode.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
@@ -1386,6 +1386,14 @@ std::vector<LayerFE::LayerSettings> Output::generateClientCompositionRequests(
                 results = layerFE.prepareClientCompositionList(targetSettings);
                 if (realContentIsVisible && !results.empty()) {
                     layer->editState().clientCompositionTimestamp = systemTime();
+                }
+
+                // Force UNKNOWN source dataspace to V0_SRGB for proper YUV-to-RGB
+                // conversion. Vendor camera HAL and video decoder often output
+                // NV12 with UNKNOWN dataspace, causing wrong color conversion.
+                for (auto& result : results) {
+                    if (result.sourceDataspace == ui::Dataspace::UNKNOWN) {
+                        result.sourceDataspace = ui::Dataspace::V0_SRGB;
+                    }
                 }
             }
 
